  "qualifications": [
    "Writers are killed by process termination after a flush, not by power loss: no claim of hardware power-loss survival.",
    "Windows does not fsync directories (durable_outbox module docstring); the POSIX path is exercised by the WSL full suite at the final head (qualification.json).",
    "Residual, accepted by Codex Checkpoint C pass 1 (#454 comment 6543744451): when a dead writer's final committed batch was its withheld tail alone, recovery has nothing to resend, so that tail's segment stays locally; the ledger holds the record and nothing is lost. The drain counts that tail as pending and its damaged bytes separately, and warns on its age; it does not imply catch-up, and no ledger probe runs on every orphan pass."
  ],
